          "id": "SP_LAROCHEOPSIS_MACROSTOMA_GEIGER_B_A_MARSHALL_2012",
          "name": "Larocheopsis macrostoma Geiger & B.A.Marshall, 2012",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Larocheopsis",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Shell medium size (to 1.2 mm. Fig. 26), trochiform, depressed. Protoconch of 0.75 whorl, smooth, no apertural varix, apertural margin sinusoid. Teleoconch of 1.66 whorls, suture little impressed. Sculpture of first 1.5 whorls consisting of pits, shoulder of last portion with distinct commarginal axial cords, crossed by approximately 8 irregularly-spaced, indistinct spiral threads. Base from periphery to closed umbilicus with up to 16 low, spiral steps, starting after 0.66 teleoconch whorl. Umbilicus closed, covered by callus. Aperture elongate, Dshaped oval, roof overhanging. Animal unknown.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:6787883",
